# Pinned upstream sources for schemas, errors, and RSA keys.
#
# The API schema base is mtcute's published layer 229 JSON. mtcute has not
# published a layer 230 schema yet, so api-schema.json was rebased onto the
# mtcute 229 JSON (which also restored messageActionChatJoinedViaCommunity,
# a mid-layer 229 addition the previous pin predates) and then surgically
# patched from tdesktop's api.tl (layer 230): constructor IDs, arguments,
# predicates, and vector modifiers were derived from the TL text, while
# existing comments, int53 annotations, union comments, throws, and
# availability from the mtcute pin were preserved entry-by-entry. The
# MTProto schema, error list, and RSA keys are unchanged upstream and
# remain pinned to mtcute.
#
# Verification: the layer 230 TL was cross-checked entry-for-entry against
# tdlib's independent layer 230 scheme (identical IDs and definitions for
# all shared entries), the mtcute base was field-by-field cross-checked
# against the final layer 229 TL (11d18d82), and the patched JSON was
# field-by-field cross-checked against the layer 230 TL. CRC32 was
# recomputed over every canonical definition for information: entries
# whose IDs do not recompute carry historically-minted IDs (Telegram keeps
# IDs across wire-compatible edits, e.g. username gained flags without a
# new ID), which is why cross-referencing two independent official
# schemes is used as ground truth instead.
tdesktop_repository=https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop
tdesktop_commit=d36272b193057a114ef3a9fe7f15a8f8b587c489
tdesktop_schema_source=Telegram/SourceFiles/mtproto/scheme/api.tl
tdesktop_derivation=schema/_old229.tl + schema/_new230.tl diff applied to the mtcute 229 JSON
tdesktop_cross_check=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tdlib/td/master/td/generate/scheme/telegram_api.tl

